MID_SE_Max_Buc_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_001: Maxim, what is so important about this conversation\nthat we must have it so late at night?
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_002: It's... Well, it's a question I've been meaning to ask\nyou for a while.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_003: With things so dire, I figured, now or never.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_004: Hm?
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_005: How can you fight by Bertrand's side?
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_006: I mean, I was his squire... I was there for the Siege\nof Cydonia.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_007: Ah... I see. All those years ago...you were that\ngreenhorn from Arago. I thought you looked familiar.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_008: Yes. And I'm sorry. I'll never be able to atone for\ntaking part in it.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_009: The looting, the brutality. Killing the viceroy...
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_010: You were a squire. You could do nothing. \nThere is no apology for you to make.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_011: But I was there—I watched it unfold. My hands\naren't clean, and they never will be.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_012: No. Look at me, Maxim.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_013: What I meant to say is, you should not torment\nyourself over what happened.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_014: Besides, who am I to accept an apology. I could not\neven stop milady from giving over her life to revenge.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_015: Buccar...
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_016: But to answer your question... I joined this war\nbecause milady wills it. I do as she asks. That is all.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_017: And besides, to be a knight means one must stand\nbeside former enemies at times. That's how it is.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_018: I'll be honest...though this does not align with\nLady Leda's opinion...
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_019: I, myself, have never thought badly of Bertrand,\neven after the Cydonia Massacre.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_020: What? How is that possible?
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_021: Lord Guillermo fought as a warrior, and Bertrand\ngave him an end befitting a warrior.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_022: Though this world is in crisis, I'm glad fate has\nallowed us to fight alongside one another.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_C_023: Right... Me too. And as Bertrand's knight, I'll gladly\nstand with you in battle.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Max_Buc_B_001: We did it, Buccar. We've won the day—and kept\nlosses to a minimum.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_B_002: That's because we are at our best when we fight as\none. I put on a bold show to draw the enemies in...
MID_SE_Max_Buc_B_003: While I evacuate the villagers, shore up our front\nline, and head out to support you.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_B_004: I'm just in awe of how you can charge into a fight\nwith no hesitation... Something I need to learn.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_B_005: I fought without hesitation because I knew you had\nmy back. It was you who allowed me to move boldly.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_B_006: Maxim, I also want to thank you for allowing me to\nspeak freely about my feelings. It was...helpful.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_B_007: I'm not sure about that. I was just trying to\nunburden myself.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_B_008: In truth, until we spoke that day, I had found it...\ndistressing...to interact with you.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_B_009: I was terribly impressed by how admirably you\nserved your duty to Bertrand as his knight...
MID_SE_Max_Buc_B_010: Hm? But, Buccar, you're just as loyal a knight\nto Leda.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_B_011: I am no longer a knight. I am nothing. My lord is\ngone, and I am just a dusty relic at milady's side.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_B_012: I have clung to Lord Guillermo's final order so I have\nsome toehold on a purpose. That is all.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_B_013: I get it... You lost your lord that day.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_B_014: But that doesn't make you any less of a knight—\nor any less admirable.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_B_015: Even after he's gone, you stay devoted to\nserving him. That speaks to the spirit of a knight.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_B_016: Hm!
MID_SE_Max_Buc_B_017: I'm young. I'm inexperienced. And I'm in awe of how\nloyal you've been. It means I have a ways to go.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_B_018: I see. Hearing these things from a knight such as\nyou...perhaps I can find some pride in myself.
MID_SE_Max_Buc_B_019: Besides, the Demon Bear of Baphos can't be caught \nwhining in front of a young knight, now can he?
MID_SE_Max_Buc_B_020: Well, in that case, here's to working together—and to\nloyally serving our lords.